cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the manuscript."
title: "PRISM-J: precision structural, phylogenomic and interactomic mapping of J-domain proteins"
abstract: "A four-layer, low-cost computational pipeline that separates conservation of the Hsp70-coupling module of a J-domain protein from the chemistry of its client and from its cellular context, and applies the separation to the chaperone control of CPEB3 functional amyloid."
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - functional amyloid
  - J-domain protein
  - CPEB3
  - Orb2
  - coarse-grained simulation
  - chaperone specificity
